What are Robot Sensors?
Robot sensors are sophisticated electronic components that enable robotic systems to perceive, interpret, and interact with their surrounding environment. These devices mimic human sensory capabilities by providing critical data on position, force, vision, touch, and various environmental factors. The market primarily serves industrial automation applications, with key sensor categories including vision sensors, movement sensors, touch sensors, and voice recognition systems.
These sensors range from proximity and vision sensors to force/torque, tactile, and ultrasonic variants, all essential for enabling robotic perception, adaptability, and precision. As robots increasingly operate in dynamic, unstructured environments, sensor technology continues evolving to offer higher accuracy, real-time feedback, and seamless integration with advanced control systems.
